> Simple example: default-box shapes and order

SSD predicts class scores and one four-offset box correction for every default
box at several feature resolutions. Each cell has a square of side s, a square
of side `sqrt(s*next_s)`, and wide/tall reciprocal-ratio pairs. Four-default cells
use ratio 2; six-default cells also use ratio 3. Order is level, row, column,
then square/geometric/wide/tall shapes, matching the convolutional head layout.
Default boxes may cross the image boundary; decoding clips them later.

The first SSD300 cell is centred at `(4,4)`. Its four shapes below use side 21
and geometric-mean side `sqrt(21*45)`. Full grids 38/19/10/5/3/1 contain 8732
boxes; the compact 64-pixel variant uses grids 16/8/4/2/1/1 and 1536 boxes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ssd_defaults.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto full =
      m::SsdDefaultBoxes({38, 19, 10, 5, 3, 1}, {21, 45, 99, 153, 207, 261, 315},
                         {8, 16, 32, 64, 100, 300}, {4, 6, 6, 6, 4, 4}, n::DType::Float64);
  const auto compact = m::SsdDefaultBoxes({16, 8, 4, 2, 1, 1}, {8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 80},
                                          {4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 64}, {4, 6, 6, 6, 4, 4});
  if (full.shape() != n::Shape{8732, 4} || compact.shape() != n::Shape{1536, 4})
    return 1;
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  const std::vector<std::string> names = {"square", "geometric", "wide 2:1", "tall 1:2"};
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colours = {
      {37, 99, 235}, {234, 88, 12}, {22, 163, 74}, {220, 38, 38}};
  for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
    const double y1 = full.at({i, 0}), x1 = full.at({i, 1}), y2 = full.at({i, 2}),
                 x2 = full.at({i, 3});
    p.lines({x1, x2, x2, x1, x1}, {y1, y1, y2, y2, y1}, names[i], colours[i]);
  }
  p.title("Four defaults at the first cell")
      .x_label("pixel x")
      .y_label("pixel y")
      .x_limits(-20, 45)
      .y_limits(-20, 45);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  p.size(900, 900).margins(90, 30, 60, 60).save_svg("build/ssd_defaults.svg");
  const auto centers = n::boxes_to_center(n::slice_axis(full, 0, 0, 4));
  if (std::abs(centers.at({0, 0}) - 4) > 1e-12 ||
      std::abs(centers.at({1, 2}) - std::sqrt(21. * 45)) > 1e-12)
    return 1;
  std::print("8732 full and 1536 compact defaults. First centre (4,4), square side21, "
             "geometric side{:.6f}; wide/tall width-height ratios2/.5. Negative corners are "
             "intentional unclipped defaults.\n",
             centers.at({1, 2}));
}
