> Conclusion

The initialized full model has 26285486 learned scalars and 71 finite, nonzero
learned tensor gradients. The compact model fits 1167362 scalars in 512 Adam
updates, selecting epoch 18 at validation AP50 0.310301. On eight test scenes/23
digits, AP50/AP75/AP50:95 are 0.203434/0.069719/0.089794, with 105 detections.
Its selected mean L2 scale is 10.035564, confirming that rescaling participates
in optimization. Detection quality remains limited in this bounded fit; the
actual gallery retains mistakes and does not imply paper-level accuracy.

Default shapes/order, 3-4-5 rescaling and the complete mined loss/derivatives are checked before fitting. The initialized full SSD300 verifies all8732 predictions and every learned tensor gradient; it is not presented as a trained benchmark. The compact model then fits visibly with learned scale parameters and validation-only checkpoint selection, retaining actual held-out mistakes in its gallery.

> References

- [Liu et al. (2016), SSD: Single Shot MultiBox Detector](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.02325).
- [TorchVision official SSD implementation](https://github.com/pytorch/vision/blob/main/torchvision/models/detection/ssd.py).
- [COCO official box evaluator](https://github.com/cocodataset/cocoapi/blob/master/PythonAPI/pycocotools/cocoeval.py).
